Changes in v8:
- snapshot the RX-ring correlator once in deliver_frame; pass
  that value through get_buffer, the room check, and harvest.
  A second DMA load must not index a pool get_buffer did not
  validate. rxq_harvest_buffer() becomes rxq_harvest_correlator()
  taking that value; KUnit tests pass it
- drop the copybreak new_skb leak fix: now done by the fixes
  series (patch 4, "ibmveth: step past bad RX correlators
  instead of spinning or oopsing"); deliver_frame keeps fix 4's
  dev_kfree_skb_any() and rx_dropped
- skip_bad_correlator, recycle_invalid (any harvest failure) and
  deliver_frame harvest failures count rx_dropped, as fix 4 does.
  skip_bad_correlator's own "bad correlator" log is dropped; the
  harvest logs the correlator once
- restore the PHYP MSS (skb->data + 8) and 0xffff comments
- rxq_harvest_correlator keeps the previous patch's reset on a bad
  correlator, so recycle_invalid resets too; commit message no
  longer says skip_bad_correlator alone owns reset
- poll re-arm comment cites close(), not a resize path and an
  interrupt WARN that are not in the tree; skip_bad_correlator
  comment no longer blames resize
- commit message: drop the NULL-skb reset and copybreak leak
  claims (fix 4 has both); a bad slot no longer ends the loop
- noted: poll_stopping is not a close barrier; mask stays first

Changes in v7:
- bound oversize against min(skb_tailroom, pool->buff_size);
  name that bound in the commit message
- noted: poll_stopping stays mask-first; skip vs budget stays;
  cancel_work stays in P10

Changes in v6:
- read the IPv4 header check through skb->data, as mainline does.
  v5 used ip_hdr(), which reads the network header offset that
  eth_type_trans() does not set on this path
- do not complete NAPI or consume budget when budget is 0. That is
  the netpoll case, where v5 completed and returned budget - 1,
  underflowing to -1
- noted: the split is not pure motion; the body lists what changed

Changes in v5:
- Wrap poll_stopping return after complete so it stays under 80 cols
- On poll_stopping after the budget loop: return < budget after
  napi_complete_done (was frames_processed-1 even when under budget)
- New in v5: peel SQ poll harden + helpers before MQ enable so tip P10
  stays bring-up focused (mailed v4 09/14 MQ enable -> tip P10; also
  14->15). Kitchen-sink / enable-path poll fixes land here on the live
  single-queue path first.
- After napi_complete_done, check poll_stopping again before enable_irq
  (avoid re-arm while resize/close waits on napi_disable)
